{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01GV7npecWeqWamKdwyrQv7w","type":"tool_result","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Perfect! Now let me compile a comprehensive report with all the key metrics:\n\n## Summary: ML Research Project Experiment Results\n\nI've explored the contamcal-irt-calibration project and located concrete metrics from multiple completed experiments. Here's the current state of experiments:\n\n---\n\n### **EXP-004: Simulation Identifiability Sweep** ✓ COMPLETED (48/120 runs)\n**Status**: 40% complete; strong evidence collected on γ (contamination parameter) recovery\n\n**Key Metrics**:\n- **γ Recovery Accuracy**: RMSE ≤ 0.04 (N=20), ≤ 0.005 (N=100) across AUC levels 0.55-0.80\n- **100% Detection Power**: All 48 runs have 95% CI excluding zero (γ ≠ 0 is detectable even at AUC=0.55)\n- **Precision Scaling**: Follows O(1/√N) pattern; CI width ratio 0.656 when N goes 20→50 (expected 0.632, deviation +3.8%)\n- **Coverage**: 80-90% at N=20; reaches 100% at N=100 (slightly below nominal at small N)\n- **MCMC Quality**: 0 divergences, max R̂=1.010, min ESS=439\n\n**Notable Finding**: Higher-AUC exposure (0.80) **increases posterior uncertainty** by 1.87-1.95× compared to AUC=0.55, suggesting collinearity between exposure and ability makes γ harder to identify (counterintuitive).\n\n---\n\n### **EXP-005: Noise Propagation Analysis** ✓ COMPLETED (25/25 fits)\n**Status**: Appendix robustness check; measurement error model robust to noise\n\n**Key Metrics**:\n- **CI Width**: Stable across noise levels (σ_e=0.1 to 1.0): CI width = 0.0997-0.1000\n- **Measurement Error Model**: ME model successfully propagates uncertainty; Rhat values consistent\n- **Conclusion**: Calibrated scores are robust to measurement noise in exposure estimates\n\n---\n\n### **EXP-006: IRT Calibration (Oracle Dosage)** ✓ PARTIALLY COMPLETED\n**Status**: GSM8K oracle (v2 MCMC in progress); ARC S1-only pooled completed\n\n**Key Results**:\n\n#### **ARC Oracle Pooled (S1-only)**:\n| Metric | Value |\n|--------|-------|\n| **γ (contamination parameter)** | **-1.464** (95% CI: [-2.51, -0.41]) |\n| Direction | **Negative** (contamination *decreases* ARC scores in 0.5B) |\n| Posterior predictive p-value (PPP) | 0.968 |\n| Diagnostics | R̂=1.010, ESS=770, 0 divergences ✓ |\n| **IRT MAE** | 0.035 (vs B0 raw 0.059) |\n| Coverage @ 95% | 62.5% (collapsed vs baseline 62.5%) |\n| Kendall τ | 0.756 |\n\n#### **GSM8K Oracle Pooled (S1-only)**:\n| Metric | Value |\n|--------|-------|\n| **γ** | 0.187 (95% CI: [-0.92, 1.33]) |\n| CI excludes zero? | **No** (weak signal) |\n| Diagnostics | R̂=1.015, ESS=330 ✗ (below threshold) |\n| PPP | 0.336 (reasonable) |\n\n#### **S1-only vs Oracle Exposure**:\n- **ARC**: Gamma nearly identical (-1.464 vs -1.46) — S1 embedding signal alone captures contamination effect\n- **GSM8K**: Gamma collapses to 0.19 (from oracle 3.77) — S1 insufficient for open-ended math tasks\n- **Implication**: Signal-type matters; contamination is benchmark-dependent\n\n#### **Baseline Comparison** (ARC):\n| Method | MAE | ECE | Coverage 95% | Kendall τ |\n|--------|-----|-----|-------------|-----------|\n| B0 Raw | 0.059 | 0.059 | 62.5% | 0.800 |\n| B4 Linear Regression | 0.056 | 0.056 | 87.5% | 0.756 |\n| **IRT 4PL+γ** | **0.035** | **0.032** | **62.5%** | **0.756** |\n| B6 DCR Fuzzy | 0.245 | 0.245 | 37.5% | 0.378 |\n\n---\n\n### **EXP-008: Signal Survival Analysis** ✓ CODE COMPLETE (dry-run pass)\n**Status**: Code ready; awaiting model regime data\n\n**Key Finding**:\n- **No signal survives across all dosage regimes** with AUC > 0.6\n  - S1 (Embedding): strong at d005 (AUC=0.99) but collapses at d100 (AUC=0.50)\n  - S2 (Min-K++): never survives (AUC~0.50 across all dosages)\n  - S4 (SelfCritique): weak throughout (AUC~0.50)\n- **Interpretation**: Single-signal detection fails; validates need for IRT multi-signal fusion\n\n---\n\n### **Critical Findings Summary** (from memory.md):\n\n1. **Delta Exposure Fix** (D037): Subtraction of d000 baseline before IRT fitting fixes Rhat from 1.53→1.01, ESS from 7→522\n2. **Negative Gamma is Real**: Not a bug; confirmed by multiple independent measurements:\n   - Raw accuracy: 0.5B ARC d000=46.9% → d100=29% (−17pp)\n   - Per-benchmark IRT: gamma=-1.46\n   - S1-only pooled IRT: gamma=-1.46\n   - 2PL ablation: PPP=0.0 (2PL also can't fit ARC)\n3. **Scale-Dependent Effects**: \n   - 0.5B: catastrophic degradation on ARC (−17pp)\n   - 1.5B+: MC benchmarks immune to contamination (<1.5pp change)\n   - HumanEval: strong dose-response at all scales (+17.7pp at 1.5B)\n4. **Multi-seed Strategy**: seed=42 + seed=123, targeting N_models~30 for statistical power\n\n---\n\n### **Paper Framing Pivot** (D038 - Latest):\n**Shift from \"calibration method\" → \"detection + benchmark-dependent characterization\"**\n- Core evidence: IRT γ shows benchmark-specific effects (GSM8K +3.77, ARC −1.46)\n- Coverage collapses to 18-33% when γ is significant → not actionable for direct score correction\n- Novelty: First systematic IRT analysis of contamination as **benchmark-heterogeneous, scale-dependent phenomenon**\n\n---\n\n### **File Paths for Reference**:\n- Registry: `/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-idea_gen_0509_13/projects/contamcal-irt-calibration/registry.yaml`\n- Report (latest status): `/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-idea_gen_0509_13/projects/contamcal-irt-calibration/report.md`\n- Memory (detailed findings): `/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-idea_gen_0509_13/projects/contamcal-irt-calibration/memory.md`\n- Exp-004 analysis: `/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-idea_gen_0509_13/projects/contamcal-irt-calibration/artifacts/exp004_incremental_analysis.md`\n- Exp-005 results: `/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-idea_gen_0509_13/projects/contamcal-irt-calibration/results/exp005/exp005_run.log`\n- Dream registry (framing iterations): `/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-idea_gen_0509_13/projects/contamcal-irt-calibration/dream_registry.yaml`\n- Literature survey: `/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-idea_gen_0509_13/projects/contamcal-irt-calibration/artifacts/literature_survey_negative_gamma.md`\n\nThe project is actively collecting evidence for a novel finding about contamination-induced performance degradation as a benchmark and scale-dependent phenomenon, with IRT used as the detection framework."}]}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"656feef8-1f1e-423a-a936-6b6196c229f5","uuid":"e454f9f3-7acc-43e2-9a0f-0c3024175acd","timestamp":"2026-05-15T05:46:24.369Z","tool_use_result":{"status":"completed","prompt":"I need to understand the current state of experiments in this ML research project. Please find and read:\n\n1. Any experiment result files, especially for exp-004 (simulation sweep), exp-005 (noise propagation), exp-006 (IRT calibration), exp-008 (signal survival)\n2. The registry or results directory structure\n3. Any analysis notebooks or summary files\n\nFocus on finding concrete metrics and results that have already been collected. The project is at /home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-idea_gen_0509_13\n\nSearch broadly - check directories like results/, experiments/, exp004/, exp006/, analysis/, etc.","agentId":"a85e543a3c4393f23","agentType":"Explore","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Perfect! Now let me compile a comprehensive report with all the key metrics:\n\n## Summary: ML Research Project Experiment Results\n\nI've explored the contamcal-irt-calibration project and located concrete metrics from multiple completed experiments. Here's the current state of experiments:\n\n---\n\n### **EXP-004: Simulation Identifiability Sweep** ✓ COMPLETED (48/120 runs)\n**Status**: 40% complete; strong evidence collected on γ (contamination parameter) recovery\n\n**Key Metrics**:\n- **γ Recovery Accuracy**: RMSE ≤ 0.04 (N=20), ≤ 0.005 (N=100) across AUC levels 0.55-0.80\n- **100% Detection Power**: All 48 runs have 95% CI excluding zero (γ ≠ 0 is detectable even at AUC=0.55)\n- **Precision Scaling**: Follows O(1/√N) pattern; CI width ratio 0.656 when N goes 20→50 (expected 0.632, deviation +3.8%)\n- **Coverage**: 80-90% at N=20; reaches 100% at N=100 (slightly below nominal at small N)\n- **MCMC Quality**: 0 divergences, max R̂=1.010, min ESS=439\n\n**Notable Finding**: Higher-AUC exposure (0.80) **increases posterior uncertainty** by 1.87-1.95× compared to AUC=0.55, suggesting collinearity between exposure and ability makes γ harder to identify (counterintuitive).\n\n---\n\n### **EXP-005: Noise Propagation Analysis** ✓ COMPLETED (25/25 fits)\n**Status**: Appendix robustness check; measurement error model robust to noise\n\n**Key Metrics**:\n- **CI Width**: Stable across noise levels (σ_e=0.1 to 1.0): CI width = 0.0997-0.1000\n- **Measurement Error Model**: ME model successfully propagates uncertainty; Rhat values consistent\n- **Conclusion**: Calibrated scores are robust to measurement noise in exposure estimates\n\n---\n\n### **EXP-006: IRT Calibration (Oracle Dosage)** ✓ PARTIALLY COMPLETED\n**Status**: GSM8K oracle (v2 MCMC in progress); ARC S1-only pooled completed\n\n**Key Results**:\n\n#### **ARC Oracle Pooled (S1-only)**:\n| Metric | Value |\n|--------|-------|\n| **γ (contamination parameter)** | **-1.464** (95% CI: [-2.51, -0.41]) |\n| Direction | **Negative** (contamination *decreases* ARC scores in 0.5B) |\n| Posterior predictive p-value (PPP) | 0.968 |\n| Diagnostics | R̂=1.010, ESS=770, 0 divergences ✓ |\n| **IRT MAE** | 0.035 (vs B0 raw 0.059) |\n| Coverage @ 95% | 62.5% (collapsed vs baseline 62.5%) |\n| Kendall τ | 0.756 |\n\n#### **GSM8K Oracle Pooled (S1-only)**:\n| Metric | Value |\n|--------|-------|\n| **γ** | 0.187 (95% CI: [-0.92, 1.33]) |\n| CI excludes zero? | **No** (weak signal) |\n| Diagnostics | R̂=1.015, ESS=330 ✗ (below threshold) |\n| PPP | 0.336 (reasonable) |\n\n#### **S1-only vs Oracle Exposure**:\n- **ARC**: Gamma nearly identical (-1.464 vs -1.46) — S1 embedding signal alone captures contamination effect\n- **GSM8K**: Gamma collapses to 0.19 (from oracle 3.77) — S1 insufficient for open-ended math tasks\n- **Implication**: Signal-type matters; contamination is benchmark-dependent\n\n#### **Baseline Comparison** (ARC):\n| Method | MAE | ECE | Coverage 95% | Kendall τ |\n|--------|-----|-----|-------------|-----------|\n| B0 Raw | 0.059 | 0.059 | 62.5% | 0.800 |\n| B4 Linear Regression | 0.056 | 0.056 | 87.5% | 0.756 |\n| **IRT 4PL+γ** | **0.035** | **0.032** | **62.5%** | **0.756** |\n| B6 DCR Fuzzy | 0.245 | 0.245 | 37.5% | 0.378 |\n\n---\n\n### **EXP-008: Signal Survival Analysis** ✓ CODE COMPLETE (dry-run pass)\n**Status**: Code ready; awaiting model regime data\n\n**Key Finding**:\n- **No signal survives across all dosage regimes** with AUC > 0.6\n  - S1 (Embedding): strong at d005 (AUC=0.99) but collapses at d100 (AUC=0.50)\n  - S2 (Min-K++): never survives (AUC~0.50 across all dosages)\n  - S4 (SelfCritique): weak throughout (AUC~0.50)\n- **Interpretation**: Single-signal detection fails; validates need for IRT multi-signal fusion\n\n---\n\n### **Critical Findings Summary** (from memory.md):\n\n1. **Delta Exposure Fix** (D037): Subtraction of d000 baseline before IRT fitting fixes Rhat from 1.53→1.01, ESS from 7→522\n2. **Negative Gamma is Real**: Not a bug; confirmed by multiple independent measurements:\n   - Raw accuracy: 0.5B ARC d000=46.9% → d100=29% (−17pp)\n   - Per-benchmark IRT: gamma=-1.46\n   - S1-only pooled IRT: gamma=-1.46\n   - 2PL ablation: PPP=0.0 (2PL also can't fit ARC)\n3. **Scale-Dependent Effects**: \n   - 0.5B: catastrophic degradation on ARC (−17pp)\n   - 1.5B+: MC benchmarks immune to contamination (<1.5pp change)\n   - HumanEval: strong dose-response at all scales (+17.7pp at 1.5B)\n4. **Multi-seed Strategy**: seed=42 + seed=123, targeting N_models~30 for statistical power\n\n---\n\n### **Paper Framing Pivot** (D038 - Latest):\n**Shift from \"calibration method\" → \"detection + benchmark-dependent characterization\"**\n- Core evidence: IRT γ shows benchmark-specific effects (GSM8K +3.77, ARC −1.46)\n- Coverage collapses to 18-33% when γ is significant → not actionable for direct score correction\n- Novelty: First systematic IRT analysis of contamination as **benchmark-heterogeneous, scale-dependent phenomenon**\n\n---\n\n### **File Paths for Reference**:\n- Registry: `/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-idea_gen_0509_13/projects/contamcal-irt-calibration/registry.yaml`\n- Report (latest status): `/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-idea_gen_0509_13/projects/contamcal-irt-calibration/report.md`\n- Memory (detailed findings): `/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-idea_gen_0509_13/projects/contamcal-irt-calibration/memory.md`\n- Exp-004 analysis: `/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-idea_gen_0509_13/projects/contamcal-irt-calibration/artifacts/exp004_incremental_analysis.md`\n- Exp-005 results: `/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-idea_gen_0509_13/projects/contamcal-irt-calibration/results/exp005/exp005_run.log`\n- Dream registry (framing iterations): `/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-idea_gen_0509_13/projects/contamcal-irt-calibration/dream_registry.yaml`\n- Literature survey: `/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-idea_gen_0509_13/projects/contamcal-irt-calibration/artifacts/literature_survey_negative_gamma.md`\n\nThe project is actively collecting evidence for a novel finding about contamination-induced performance degradation as a benchmark and scale-dependent phenomenon, with IRT used as the detection framework."}],"totalDurationMs":60802,"totalTokens":67380,"totalToolUseCount":27,"usage":{"input_tokens":5,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1126,"cache_read_input_tokens":64092,"output_tokens":2157,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":1126},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[{"input_tokens":5,"output_tokens":2157,"cache_read_input_tokens":64092,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1126,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":1126,"ephemeral_1h_input_token