{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01FwVQxuzzQAqWutchd2Nqu1","type":"tool_result","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Perfect! Now I have all the key information. Let me compile a comprehensive summary of the exp-004 simulation sweep results.\n\n## Summary of Detailed Results from Exp-004 Simulation Sweep\n\nI've located and analyzed the detailed results from the contamcal-irt-calibration exp-004 simulation sweep. Here's what I found:\n\n### Key Files Located\n\n1. **Main Analysis Document**: `/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-idea_gen_0509_13/projects/contamcal-irt-calibration/artifacts/exp004_incremental_analysis.md` (v4 status)\n2. **Backup Report**: `/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-idea_gen_0509_13/projects/contamcal-irt-calibration/artifacts/exp-004/report/exp004_incremental_analysis.md` (earlier version)\n3. **Results JSON Files**: 13 condition files in `/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-idea_gen_0509_13/projects/contamcal-irt-calibration/artifacts/simulation_sweep/results/`\n4. **Checkpoint Logs**: Multiple v2-v5 checkpoint files in the checkpoints directory\n\n### Overall Sweep Status (v4 final, v5 in progress)\n\n- **Total seeds**: 120 (4 AUC levels × 3 N_models × 10 seeds)\n- **Completed (v4)**: 48/120 runs (40.0%)\n- **Conditions completed**: AUC 0.55 (N=20,50,100), AUC 0.80 (N=20,50,100 partial)\n- **Conditions in progress**: AUC 0.65, 0.90\n\n### AUC Thresholds and Findings\n\n**AUC levels tested**: 0.55, 0.65, 0.80, 0.90 (with 0.65 and 0.90 having limited seeds)\n\n**Key Finding - AUC Effect**: Higher AUC paradoxically increases γ posterior uncertainty:\n- **CI95 width ratio (AUC=0.80 / AUC=0.55)**: 1.87-1.95× wider at high AUC\n- Mechanism: Higher-AUC exposure creates collinearity between γ·exposure and ability (θ), making it harder to disentangle exposure effect from ability\n- This ratio remains stable across N, indicating multiplicative effects\n\n### N_models Conditions and Coverage Rates\n\n**Complete N_models analysis (AUC=0.55)**:\n\n| N_models | Seeds OK | γ Bias | RMSE | CI95 Width | CI95 Coverage | Status |\n|----------|----------|--------|------|-----------|---------------|--------|\n| 20 | 10/10 | +0.020 | 0.040 | 0.133 (13.3pp) | 80% | Complete |\n| 50 | 10/10 | +0.015 | 0.026 | 0.087 (8.7pp) | 90% | Complete |\n| 100 | 7/10 | -0.003 | 0.005 | 0.065 (6.5pp) | 100% | Running |\n\n**Coverage findings**:\n- N=20: 80% coverage (5pp below nominal) — low coverage driven by positive-bias outliers\n- N=50: 90% coverage (5pp below nominal)\n- N=100: 100% coverage achieved\n- **Recommendation**: Use N≥50 for reliable coverage\n\n### Identifiability Results (v4 Complete Data)\n\n**γ Identifiability Confirmed Across All Conditions**:\n- All 48 completed runs have CI95 excluding zero (100% power)\n- Smallest CI lower bound: 0.208 (outlier at AUC=0.80, N=20, seed 6 with bias -0.172)\n- Even worst-case decisively rejects γ=0\n\n**1/√N Scaling Verified**:\n- CI width ratios match theoretical √(N₁/N₂) within 4% per transition\n- Cumulative deviation: n20→n100 is 8.4% (indicates small prior variance floor)\n- Excellent predictive power for sample size planning\n\n### MCMC Quality Metrics (48 completed runs)\n\n- Total divergences: 0 / 48 runs\n- Maximum R̂: 1.010 (all runs well-mixed)\n- Minimum ESS: 439 (seed 1, auc0.55_n20) — adequate mixing\n- Highly reliable parameter recovery\n\n### AUC=0.80 Special Case (Counterintuitive Finding)\n\n**Higher AUC means harder recovery**:\n\n| Condition | N_models | CI95 Width | Posterior SD | Ratio to AUC=0.55 |\n|-----------|----------|-----------|---------|-----------|\n| AUC=0.55 | 50 | 0.087 | 0.022 | — |\n| AUC=0.80 | 50 | 0.163 | 0.041 | **1.87×** |\n| AUC=0.55 | 100 | 0.065 | 0.016 | — |\n| AUC=0.80 | 100 | 0.116 | 0.029 | **1.81×** |\n\nThis counterintuitive result (better exposure signal → harder γ recovery) is stable and **confirmed** across multiple N levels.\n\n### Version History (v2-v5 Checkpoint Analysis)\n\n- **v2**: 46/120 completed, then crashed\n- **v3**: Attempted resume with TMPDIR fix, 0 auc0.65 successful\n- **v4**: Clean retry from checkpoint, achieved 48/120, v4 marked \"failed\" due to process death\n- **v5**: Continuation of v4 (98/120 processed, 68 successful), auc0.65 conditions systematically failing\n\n**Failure Pattern**: auc0.65 conditions consistently fail across v3-v5, suggesting numerical instability near AUC=0.65.\n\n### Computation Times\n\n| Condition | Avg Time/Seed |\n|-----------|---------------|\n| AUC=0.55, N=20 | 321s (~5 min) |\n| AUC=0.55, N=50 | 1,295s (~22 min) |\n| AUC=0.55, N=100 | 3,793s (~63 min) |\n| AUC=0.80, N=100 | 4,783s (~80 min) |\n| AUC=0.90, N=50 | ~1,800s (estimated) |\n\n### AUC Threshold Estimate\n\nCannot definitively determine threshold yet:\n- AUC=0.55: CI width ≤13.3pp (below 15pp threshold)\n- AUC=0.80: CI width 11.6-16.3pp (marginal, depends on N)\n- AUC=0.90: CI width ~20.7pp at N=50 (exceeds threshold)\n- **Next step**: AUC=0.65 and 0.90 data completion would map full landscape\n\n### Paper-Ready Claims Status\n\n1. **γ identifiable across signal strengths**: STRONG (100% power, RMSE ≤0.04)\n2. **Precision scales as 1/√N**: STRONG (verified within 5% across transitions)\n3. **Exposure-ability collinearity inflates γ posterior**: STRONG & COUNTERINTUITIVE (1.87-1.95× ratio stable)\n4. **Robust detection power**: STRONG (48/48 runs detect γ≠0)\n5. **Coverage below nominal at small N**: MODERATE (80-90% at N=20, needs more validation)\n6. **Bias direction reversal**: DOWNGRADED to weak observation (not statistically significant)\n\n### File Locations\n\n- Analysis doc: `/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-idea_gen_0509_13/projects/contamcal-irt-calibration/artifacts/exp004_incremental_analysis.md`\n- Results directory: `/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-idea_gen_0509_13/projects/contamcal-irt-calibration/artifacts/simulation_sweep/results/`\n- Individual condition JSONs: `auc{0.55,0.65,0.8,0.9}_n{20,50,100}_prior1.0_binary.json`\n- Checkpoints: 